course: dictionary
lesson: 1981
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one. «Composition» can mean what something is made of, a piece of music, or a short school essay. Look at the words around it to pick the right meaning.
explain: «Handwriting (presentation) and composition (what is written and how well) are different skills and are marked separately.» Here composition is about the words you write and how good they are, not about the paper or the ink. Ask yourself: what is being judged?
explain: In a sentence about music or art, composition means a piece someone has created. «SONG BY TOAD, OTHER COMPOSITIONS BY TOAD» shows that a composition can be a piece of music or other work made by a person, here Toad himself.
fact: Composition means what something is made of, and how much of each part there is, as in the composition of air.
fact: Composition can mean a piece of music, art or writing that someone has created.
fact: Composition can also mean a short school essay, an old-fashioned use common in the UK.
fact: In a photo, composition means the way the parts of the picture are arranged.
fact: In maths, composition of numbers shows a number built from parts, such as 25 = 20 + 5.
exercise: «Handwriting and composition are marked separately.» In this sentence, what does composition mean? | The colour of the ink | Neat letters and joined-up writing | A piece of music | *What is written and how well it is written
exercise: What does «the composition of air» mean? | How cold the air feels on a winter day | The way air moves around the world | A song about the wind | *What air is made of and how much of each part there is
exercise: «SONG BY TOAD, OTHER COMPOSITIONS BY TOAD.» What does composition mean in this list? | What something is made of | How the parts of a picture are arranged | A short school essay | *A piece of music or other work someone has created
test: In maths, 25 = 20 + 5 shows which idea? | *Composition of numbers, 25 built from parts | Measuring the length of a line | Subtraction, taking one number from another | Rounding 25 to the nearest ten
test: In a photo, what does composition mean? | The name of the photographer | What the camera cost | How bright the photo is | *How the parts of the picture are arranged
exam: Which meaning fits «a composer writes compositions»? | What something is made of | How a photo is arranged | *A piece of music someone has created | A short school essay
